Appendix - wget and ffmpeg Support
----------------------------------

The SoX Windows binary can make use of the wget command line utility
to load files over the internet and of the ffmpeg utility to read
an extra four dozen audio and video formats.

Binary copies of wget and ffmpeg have been included with this package
for your convenience.

For SoX to make use of wget or ffmpeg, they must be located either
in your PATH or within the same directory that SoX is run from.

Custom configuration of wget can be made by editing the file wget.ini
contained in the same directory as wget.exe.

Please consult wget and ffmpeg's homepages for access to source code
as well as further instructions on configuring them.

http://www.gnu.org/software/wget
http://ffmpeg.org

Appendix - MP3 and AMR-NB/AMR-WB Support
----------------------------------------

Now that the MP3 patents have expired and the opencore AMR libraries
are free, SoX contains support for reading and writing these files.

Appendix - LADSPA Plugins
-------------------------

SoX has built-in support for LADSPA Plugins; see http://www.ladspa.org

SoX will search for these plugins based on the LADSPA_PATH
environment variable.  See sox_ng.txt for further information.
